e1 (primary), node2, and node3 (standbys) on Alpine Linux. Demonstrated a full failover: killed node1 (primary), promoted node2 to writable primary with zero committed-data loss, repointed node3 to follow node2, then rebuilt node1 as a standby of node2 via pg_basebackup once pg_rewind proved infeasible (source WAL segment already recycled). Final topology: node2 primary, node1 and node3 standbys, fully streaming and consistent. Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: restarted node1, node3, then node2 (the primary) one at a time via native reboot, confirming a changed OS boot_id and full PostgreSQL/data/replication recovery after each restart, preserving write availability throughout.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed postgresql16/postgresql16-contrib on node1, node2, node3 via apk\",\"Configured /etc/hosts and enabled passwordless root SSH between nodes for file transfer (unlocked locked root accounts, installed cluster SSH keys)\",\"Initialized node1 as primary via rc-service auto_setup/initdb; set wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders=10, max_replication_slots=10, hot_standby=on, listen_addresses='*'; added pg_hba.conf rules for replication and app connections\",\"Generated a replication role and random password on node1; distributed the password file to node2/node3 via scp without ever printing it in a command\",\"Built node2 and node3 as standbys via pg_basebackup -R (creates standby.signal and primary_conninfo automatically)\",\"Created repl_test table on the primary and confirmed initial rows replicated to both standbys, then confirmed live inserts replicate with zero lag\",\"Simulated primary loss: force-stopped postgres on node1 after confirming replay_lsn matched sent_lsn on both standbys (no in-flight data)\",\"Promoted node2 to writable primary via pg_ctl promote --wait; verified pg_is_in_recovery=false and all pre-crash rows present, then wrote a new row\",\"Repointed node3's primary_conninfo to node2 via ALTER SYSTEM + restart; verified it received the post-failover row\",\"Attempted pg_rewind to reintroduce node1 as a standby of node2; aborted when the diverged WAL segment had already been recycled during node1's crash recovery\",\"Rebuilt node1 from scratch as a standby of node2 via pg_basebackup -R; verified it caught up with all rows including post-failover writes\",\"Verified final topology: node2 primary (pg_is_in_recovery=false), node1 and node3 both streaming from node2 with identical row counts\",\"Captured per-node OS boot_id and PostgreSQL/replication health as a baseline for all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and standby recovery/replication resumption\",\"Restarted node3 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and standby recovery/replication resumption\",\"Restarted node2 (the primary) via native reboot only after confirming both standbys were healthy; polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, confirmed it resumed as writable primary with all data intact and both standbys reconnected\",\"Performed a final end-to-end write/replication check across all three nodes post full rolling restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Streaming replication established: node1 primary, node2/node3 standbys, initial and live data replicated\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c4d85d4cf1234003\",\"cmd-a77d7258049b48e9\",\"cmd-4be5121ee46a424b\",\"cmd-dabbe2d1f3df4ceb\",\"cmd-eb1b6746ac25411a\",\"cmd-680fe6484c644059\",\"cmd-41d136ec017345cf\"],\"summary\":\"node1 confirmed listening/serving as primary; pg_basebackup succeeded on node2/node3; pg_stat_replication showed both streaming async with zero lag; repl_test rows matched across all three nodes after inserts on the primary\"},{\"requirement\":\"Primary failure and promotion without losing committed data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e461fb14bb44423d\",\"cmd-41d136ec017345cf\",\"cmd-6c93e75114b141d9\",\"cmd-aa855c2c5f1c4cd6\",\"cmd-6eae176de6424569\",\"cmd-dc8075c511ee4757\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed replay_lsn=sent_lsn on both standbys before crashing node1; force-stopped node1; promoted node2 via pg_ctl promote; node2 showed pg_is_in_recovery=false with all 4 pre-crash rows intact, then accepted a new write as primary\"},{\"requirement\":\"Surviving standby (node3) follows the newly promoted primary\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7b57f2c8feb54051\",\"cmd-3d9532dca3af4ac7\",\"cmd-d079d3b18d8d426e\"],\"summary\":\"node3 was still pointed at dead node1 and missing the post-failover row; after repointing primary_conninfo to node2 and restarting, node3 came up in recovery streaming from node2 and showed the post-failover row; node2's pg_stat_replication confirmed node3 connected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Recovered former primary (node1) rejoins as a standby of the current primary (node2) without data loss\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-add1b0fb4ab84723\",\"cmd-6496d47cf3824d10\",\"cmd-3062dfed663b489a\",\"cmd-240b647569ec4e16\",\"cmd-aaa38343500f468c\"],\"summary\":\"pg_rewind was attempted and found infeasible (target WAL segment already recycled); node1 was rebuilt via pg_basebackup from node2, restarted, and confirmed in recovery streaming from node2 with all rows (including post-failover writes) present; node2's replication view showed both node1 and node3 streaming\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final full-cluster consistency check after failover/recovery cycle\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-388108c61b1041a1\",\"cmd-53a3ba0a7ea44631\",\"cmd-a5f002a53fcb4fa5\"],\"summary\":\"Inserted a row on node2 (primary) and confirmed matching row counts on node1 and node3 standbys\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-34fb39e8771041c4\",\"cmd-be9d2d5991de40cc\",\"cmd-235549b3fece408a\",\"cmd-0dc625a028c84c74\",\"cmd-df0f567eb3e243ea\"],\"summary\":\"Captured baseline boot_id 9194ed7d and standby health; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-restart boot_id changed to f4fe9e17; postgres restarted, resumed as standby with all 6 rows, and reappeared in node2's pg_stat_replication\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, chang
