 489fa607; reboot acknowledged; post-restart boot_id changed to c6c74161; postgres restarted, resumed as standby with all 6 rows intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 (primary) restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state and quorum\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-634a05fa01f644de\",\"cmd-577d739a92c245f6\",\"cmd-62fcfb62796440e5\",\"cmd-59f39d1cef704a34\",\"cmd-b36f829ee90c43bc\",\"cmd-cb8b2868aacc4385\",\"cmd-534647affc5743a5\",\"cmd-cf05a381641e4c6d\"],\"summary\":\"Captured baseline boot_id aca63b09 and confirmed both standbys streaming before restarting the primary last, preserving availability; reboot acknowledged; post-restart boot_id changed to c1c6b4c6; postgres resumed as writable primary with all data intact, both standbys reconnected, and a fresh write successfully replicated to both node1 and node3\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Set up PostgreSQL 16 streaming replication across node1 (primary), node2, and node3 (standbys) on Alpine Linux. Demonstrated a full failover: killed node1 (primary), promoted node2 to writable primary with zero committed-data loss, repointed node3 to follow node2, then rebuilt node1 as a standby of node2 via pg_basebackup once pg_rewind proved infeasible (source WAL segment already recycled). Final topology: node2 primary, node1 and node3 standbys, fully streaming and consistent. Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: restarted node1, node3, then node2 (the primary) one at a time via native reboot, confirming a changed OS boot_id and full PostgreSQL/data/replication recovery after each restart, preserving write availability throughout.","actions_performed":["Installed postgresql16/postgresql16-contrib on node1, node2, node3 via apk","Configured /etc/hosts and enabled passwordless root SSH between nodes for file transfer (unlocked locked root accounts, installed cluster SSH keys)","Initialized node1 as primary via rc-service auto_setup/initdb; set wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders=10, max_replication_slots=10, hot_standby=on, listen_addresses='*'; added pg_hba.conf rules for replication and app connections","Generated a replication role and random password on node1; distributed the password file to node2/node3 via scp without ever printing it in a command","Built node2 and node3 as standbys via pg_basebackup -R (creates standby.signal and primary_conninfo automatically)","Created repl_test table on the primary and confirmed initial rows replicated to both standbys, then confirmed live inserts replicate with zero lag","Simulated primary loss: force-stopped postgres on node1 after confirming replay_lsn matched sent_lsn on both standbys (no in-flight data)","Promoted node2 to writable primary via pg_ctl promote --wait; verified pg_is_in_recovery=false and all pre-crash rows present, then wrote a new row","Repointed node3's primary_conninfo to node2 via ALTER SYSTEM + restart; verified it received the post-failover row","Attempted pg_rewind to reintroduce node1 as a standby of node2; aborted when the diverged WAL segment had already been recycled during node1's crash recovery","Rebuilt node1 from scratch as a standby of node2 via pg_basebackup -R; verified it caught up with all rows including post-failover writes","Verified final topology: node2 primary (pg_is_in_recovery=false), node1 and node3 both streaming from node2 with identical row counts","Captured per-node OS boot_id and PostgreSQL/replication health as a baseline for all three nodes","Restarted node1 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and standby recovery/replication resumption","Restarted node3 via native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and standby recovery/replication resumption","Restarted node2 (the primary) via native reboot only after confirming both standbys were healthy; polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, confirmed it resumed as writable primary with all data intact and both standbys reconnected","Performed a final end-to-end write/replication check across all three nodes post full rolling restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Streaming replication established: node1 primary, node2/node3 standbys, initial and live data replicated","command_ids":["cmd-c4d85d4cf1234003","cmd-a77d7258049b48e9","cmd-4be5121ee46a424b","cmd-dabbe2d1f3df4ceb","cmd-eb1b6746ac25411a","cmd-680fe6484c644059","cmd-41d136ec017345cf"],"summary":"node1 confirmed listening/serving as primary; pg_basebackup succeeded on node2/node3; pg_stat_replication showed both streaming async with zero lag; repl_test rows matched across all three nodes after inserts on the primary"},{"requirement":"Primary failure and promotion without losing committed data","command_ids":["cmd-e461fb14bb44423d","cmd-41d136ec017345cf","cmd-6c93e75114b141d9","cmd-aa855c2c5f1c4cd6","cmd-6eae176de6424569","cmd-dc8075c511ee4757"],"summary":"Confirmed replay_lsn=sent_lsn on both standbys before crashing node1; force-stopped node1; promoted node2 via pg_ctl promote; node2 showed pg_is_in_recovery=false with all 4 pre-crash rows intact, then accepted a new write as primary"},{"requirement":"Surviving standby (node3) follows the newly promoted primary","command_ids":["cmd-7b57f2c8feb54051","cmd-3d9532dca3af4ac7","cmd-d079d3b18d8d426e"],"summary":"node3 was still pointed at dead node1 and missing the post-failover row; after repointing primary_conninfo to node2 and restarting, node3 came up in recovery streaming from node2 and showed the post-failover row; node2's pg_stat_replication confirmed node3 connected"},{"requirement":"Recovered former primary (node1) rejoins as a standby of the current primary (node2) without data loss","command_ids":["cmd-add1b0fb4ab84723","cmd-6496d47cf3824d10","cmd-3062dfed663b489a","cmd-240b647569ec4e16","cmd-aaa38343500f468c"],"summary":"pg_rewind was attempted and found infeasible (target WAL segment already recycled); node1 was rebuilt via pg_basebackup from node2, restarted, and co